        "id": 228676,
        "name": "PlatinumWarlock",
        "username": "PlatinumWarlock",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/platinumwarlock/{size}/1869_2.png",
        "created_at": "2019-09-19T13:18:11.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I think many people are holding off on writing adventures for the time being, due to the lack of rules for villain creation (including lieutenant and minion creation).&nbsp; Also, I'm sure that a number of other GMs are waiting for additional information on how to use the scene tracker effectively, as well as other system-specific nuances that would make adventure writing much easier.</p>\n<p>In the meanwhile, I might direct you towards the Villain of the Day thread (which has a great number of interlinked-villains with implied campaign arcs), as well as the The Big Campaign Arc Thread (currently on Page 2), which has a number of 6-issue arcs laid out.</p>",
        "post_number": 2,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T06:03:14.186Z",
