        "can_wiki": false,
        "read": false,
        "user_title": null,
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "<p>While I'd love to see a broad licensing, I think the D&amp;D Community Content model is not a good one. Excessive percentages, lots of low quality content, no route to the FLGS, forfeiture of copyright rights. It's one thing to get a decent paycheck for a work for hire as a freelancer, it's another entirely to forfeit the IP for potentially trivial cash. Futher, the way the license is set up, it's very possible that they could pull a GW and go after fans' personal websites.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nI do think non-onerous licensing is a good thing, even with a fee... but most of the Community Content licenses have onerous provisions.</p>",
